IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ha-types`
IMPORT `ha-pay`
IMPORT `ha-annual`
IMPORT `ha-public`
IMPORT `ha-leave`
IMPORT `ha-enforcement`

-- Holidays Act 2003 — THE TOP-LEVEL GOAL.
--
--   "For this holiday or leave event, is the employee entitled, how much
--    must the employer pay, when, and does the employee earn an alternative
--    holiday?"
--
-- One answer through Goals 1-5 (ha-pay.l4, ha-annual.l4, ha-public.l4,
-- ha-leave.l4). Enforcement and records (Goal 6) answer their own questions
-- in ha-enforcement.l4.

§ `The top-level goal`

DECLARE `Holiday event` IS ONE OF
    `an annual holiday` HAS
        `the annual holiday taken`                      IS AN `Annual holiday`
        `agreed to be paid in the pay for the period`   IS A BOOLEAN
        `paid with pay under a valid s 28 arrangement`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the end of the employment` HAS
        `the ending`                                    IS AN `End of employment`
    `a public holiday` HAS
        `the public holiday as it fell`                 IS A `Public holiday worked or not`
    `an alternative holiday taken` HAS
        `the alternative holiday taken`                 IS AN `Alternative holiday`
    `a spell of leave` HAS
        `the leave taken`                               IS A Leave
    `a closedown` HAS
        `the closedown period`                          IS A Closedown
    `a request to cash up annual holidays` HAS
        `the payout request`                            IS A `Payout request`
    `a request to exchange an alternative holiday` HAS
        `the exchange request`                          IS AN `Exchange request`

DECLARE `Holiday pay position` HAS
    `the employee is entitled`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `amount the employer must pay`                      IS A NUMBER
    `when it is due`                                    IS A `When payment is due`
    `an alternative holiday is earned`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `entitlement used`                                  IS A NUMBER

GIVEN entitled IS A BOOLEAN, amount IS A NUMBER, due IS A `When payment is due`, alternative IS A BOOLEAN, used IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Holiday pay position`
`position` entitled amount due alternative used MEANS
    `Holiday pay position` OF entitled, amount, IF amount EQUALS 0 THEN `nothing is payable` ELSE due, alternative, used

-- s 40(3) entitles the employee "to be paid for a public holiday" in the
-- notional holiday, without saying at what rate. FORK F12: the relevant or
-- average daily pay for the last day of employment, as s 60(2)(b) uses for
-- untaken alternative holidays.
-- s 40(2)(b): only for an employee who "is entitled to annual holidays".
@ref ss 23-26, 40(3), 60(2)(b), 67, 72F
GIVEN e IS AN `End of employment`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the final holiday pay for` e MEANS
        `the annual holiday pay owed at the end of` e
    PLUS (IF e's `the employee has become entitled to annual holidays`
          THEN e's `public holidays in the notional holiday on otherwise working days` TIMES `the daily pay` (e's `daily pay on the last day of employment`)
          ELSE 0)
    PLUS `the pay for alternative holidays not taken at the end of` e
    PLUS `the pay for untaken sick or family violence leave at the end of employment`

@ref ss 21-28B, 33-34, 40, 46-61A, 63-72J
@export default The holiday pay position under the Holidays Act 2003 (NZ) for one event: an annual holiday (ss 21, 22, 27), the end of the employment (ss 23-26, 40(3), 60(2)(b)), a public holiday worked or not (ss 49, 50, 56, 59, 61A), an alternative holiday taken (ss 57, 60), a spell of sick, bereavement or family violence leave (ss 63-72J), a closedown (ss 32-35), a cash-up of annual holidays (ss 28A, 28B) or an exchange of an alternative holiday (s 61): whether the employee is entitled, the least the employer must pay, when it is due, whether an alternative holiday is earned, and how much entitlement is used. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN ev IS A `Holiday event`  @desc The event, with the facts its sections need: the holiday or leave taken, the day as it fell, the end of the employment, the closedown, or the request
GIVETH A `Holiday pay position`
`the holiday pay position for` ev MEANS
    CONSIDER ev
    WHEN `an annual holiday` h agreed s28 THEN
        `position` TRUE (`the annual holiday pay for` h)
                   (`when annual holiday pay is due, agreed to pay in the period:` agreed `, employment ended:` FALSE `, s 28 applies:` s28)
                   FALSE (h's `portion taken, in weeks`)
    WHEN `the end of the employment` e THEN
        `position` TRUE (`the final holiday pay for` e) `in the pay for the final period of employment` FALSE 0
    WHEN `a public holiday` p THEN
        `position` (p's `would otherwise be a working day for the employee` OR p's `the employee worked any part of the day under the agreement`)
                   (`the pay for the public holiday` p) `when public holiday pay is due`
                   (`the employee earns an alternative holiday for` p) 0
    WHEN `an alternative holiday taken` a THEN
        `position` (`the alternative holiday meets s 57` a) (`the pay for the alternative holiday` a)
                   `in the pay for the pay period in which the holiday or leave falls` FALSE 1
    WHEN `a spell of leave` l THEN
        `position` (lp's `entitled to the leave`) (lp's `leave pay`) (lp's `when leave pay is due`) FALSE (lp's `days deducted from the entitlement`)
        WHERE lp MEANS `the leave position for` l
    WHEN `a closedown` c THEN
        `position` (cp's `the employer may require the closedown to be taken`) (cp's `holiday pay for the closedown`)
                   `before the holiday is taken` FALSE (cp's `weeks taken as annual holidays` PLUS cp's `weeks taken as annual holidays in advance`)
        WHERE cp MEANS `the closedown position for` c
    WHEN `a request to cash up annual holidays` r THEN
        `position` (`the employer may agree to the payout` r) (`the payout for` r)
                   `as soon as practicable after the employer agrees` FALSE
                   (IF `the payout for` r GREATER THAN 0 THEN r's `weeks requested to be paid out` ELSE 0)
    WHEN `a request to exchange an alternative holiday` x THEN
        `position` (`the employee may request the exchange` x) (`the payment in exchange for the alternative holiday` x)
                   `as soon as practicable after the employer agrees` FALSE
                   (IF `the payment in exchange for the alternative holiday` x GREATER THAN 0 THEN 1 ELSE 0)
